Code
----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------

* sjettTT/tt-qwen-3.8-flash-next (Apache License 2.0), commit 79472f41. A ttnn port of Qwen3.8-Flash-Next. Its CPU
  oracle is the specification of the float32 reference in tt_qwen38/ref/model.py, and its ttnn op sequences and
  numerics notes were the recipe for the single-card device code in tt_qwen38/.

* Strata (MIT License), Copyright (c) 2026 Niko1221 and the Strata contributors (commit dbb2d168c).
  - tt_qwen38/ref/third_party/strata_gguf_reader.py and strata_tokenizer.py: copied, MIT header kept.
  - tt_qwen38/third_party/strata_mtp/: tools/mtp_fetch.py, tools/mtp_pack.py and strata_control/tls.py (import
    paths changed), which fetch and pack the MTP draft layer exactly as Strata's setup does.
  - tt_qwen38/data/expert-profile-coder.prof and expert-profile.prof (Strata's .bin files, renamed): Strata's expert-placement profiles (which experts
    are resident on the accelerator).
  The design of hot experts on an accelerator and cold experts on the CPU follows Strata's CUDA engine.
  MIT License text: third_party_licenses/Strata-MIT.txt.

* llama.cpp / ggml (MIT License), Copyright (c) 2023-2026 The ggml authors, commit aa75ff32.
  - tt_qwen38/third_party/gguf_py/gguf: llama.cpp's gguf-py (GGUF reading and writing, incl. type Q2_0).
  - native/: libhostexp.so calls ggml's CPU dot-product kernels; native/build.sh fetches and builds ggml at that
    commit (the built libraries ship in the container image and in a built tt-qwen38-native wheel).
  MIT License text: third_party_licenses/llama.cpp-ggml-MIT.txt.

* GCC's libgomp (GPL-3.0 with the GCC Runtime Library Exception) is copied next to libhostexp.so by native/build.sh
  so the library runs without a system OpenMP runtime; the Runtime Library Exception permits this.

* tt-metal / ttnn (Apache License 2.0), Copyright Tenstorrent AI ULC, commit
  58648d44443223041148125843ca7c7d4780463e (tag v0.80.0-dev20260921). This project is a client of ttnn; the container
  image contains a build of tt-metal at that commit, its models/common directory, and
  models/experimental/gated_attention_gated_deltanet, whose delta-rule ops tt_qwen38/model.py imports (tt-metal's LICENSE).

* Lottolabs and ISTA-DASLab: credit for the quantized weights above (not redistributed).
